      "question": "In which present day state will you find the Megudi temple? &#2350;&#2375;&#2327;&#2369;&#2337;&#2368; &#2350;&#2306;&#2342;&#2367;&#2352; &#2310;&#2346;&#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In which present day state will you find the Megudi temple?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2350;&#2375;&#2327;&#2369;&#2337;&#2368; &#2350;&#2306;&#2342;&#2367;&#2352; &#2310;&#2346;&#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Tamil Nadu &#2340;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2337;&#2369;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Tamil Nadu</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2337;&#2369;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Odisha &#2323;&#2337;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Odisha</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2323;&#2337;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Karnataka &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2366;&#2335;&#2325;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Karnataka</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2366;&#2335;&#2325;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Kerala &#2325;&#2375;&#2352;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Kerala</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2352;&#2354;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>\"Meguti Jain Temple\" is another remarkable temple of its kind. Located in Aihole, <b>Karnataka </b>on the Megutigudda, this temple exhibits Dravidian style of architecture. The temple stands on a hill and thus named as \"MeganaBasadi\", meaning the The Upper Temple, which in course of time was corrupted to Megudi or Meguti.</p>",
