    {
      "id": "7b4431799967-q9",
      "number": 9,
      "question": "Which of the following is the style of temple architecture that is widely favoured in northern India? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2350;&#2306;&#2342;&#2367;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2325;&#2354;&#2366; &#2358;&#2376;&#2354;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352;&#2368; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is the style of temple architecture that is widely favoured in northern India?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2350;&#2306;&#2342;&#2367;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2325;&#2354;&#2366; &#2358;&#2376;&#2354;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352;&#2368; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Vihar &#2357;&#2367;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Vihar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Madapa &#2350;&#2342;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Madapa</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2342;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Nagar &#2344;&#2327;&#2352;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Nagar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2327;&#2352;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Dravid &#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2367;&#2337;&#2364;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Dravid</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2367;&#2337;&#2364;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>The <b>Nagara</b> style is the predominant temple architecture style in <b>northern India</b>.</p><p>Key features of Nagara style:</p><p>&#183; Beehive-shaped tower called <b>shikhara</b>.</p><p>&#183; Temples are generally built on a raised platform.</p><p>&#183; Absence of elaborate boundary walls or gateways (unlike Dravidian temples).</p><p>&#183; The <b>garbhagriha</b> (sanctum sanctorum) is directly under the shikhara.</p><p><b>Further Insight: </b></p><p>&#183; <b>Vihar:</b> Refers to Buddhist monastery complexes, not a style of temple architecture.</p><p>&#183; <b>Madapa:</b> Likely a misspelling of <i>Mandapa</i>, which is a component of temples (pillared hall), not a style.</p><p>&#183; <b>Dravid:</b> Refers to Dravidian style, which is typical of southern India and includes features like pyramid-shaped towers (vimanas) and large gateway towers (gopurams).</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
